### GET request to example server
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Max",
  "lastName": "Mustermann",
  "email": "max.test@example.com",
  "password": "SichererTest",
  "phoneNumber": "+491701234567",
  "dateOfBirth": "1998-05-15",
  "licenseClass": "B",
  "licenseExpiryDate": "2032-05-15",
  "street": "Testplatz",
  "houseNumber": "1",
  "postalCode": "60439",
  "city": "Frankfurt",
  "country": "Germany"
}

### Login correct password (200 expected)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "max.mustermann@example.com",
  "password": "SichererTestPassword123!"
}

### Login incorrect pw (401)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "max.mustermann@example.com",
  "password": "falsch"
}

### Login incorrect email (401)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@example.com",
  "password": "egal"
}

### 1. Who am I (with token)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/me
Authorization: Bearer Rn9rsCmc5UUKjdDhyC0Rsg41n5SpBlezoySfpe33z4c

### 2. Who am I (without token)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/me

### 3. Logout (same token)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer Rn9rsCmc5UUKjdDhyC0Rsg41n5SpBlezoySfpe33z4c

### 4. Who am I again (same token, expect 401)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/me
Authorization: Bearer Rn9rsCmc5UUKjdDhyC0Rsg41n5SpBlezoySfpe33z4c

### 5. Logout without token (expect your OK)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/logout